//? Title: Chu–Liu/Edmonds: Contract Cycles, Recover a Rooted Directed Tree
//? Subtitle: Actual incoming choices, reduced costs, nested expansion and explicit limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A directed network needs a cheapest set of links that lets one prescribed root
reach every vertex. Choosing each vertex's cheapest incoming link can create
cycles disconnected from the root. Chu–Liu/Edmonds contracts those cycles,
solves the reduced problem and expands the selected links back to the original
graph. We retain the original three-vertex example, follow actual nested
contractions, verify a controlled cycle family, and distinguish nonexistence,
work caps and numerical range failures. Canonical C++ now recovers original
edge identities and records the executing kernel's phases without replay.
)

\toc

> The original three vertices: cheap incoming arcs form a cycle

Root 0 has arcs 0→1 of cost 5 and 0→2 of cost 6. The two other arcs,
1→2 and 2→1, each cost 1. Independently choosing the cheapest incoming arc
for vertices 1 and 2 selects both unit arcs. Their total 2 is a lower bound,
but those arcs form a cycle and neither vertex is reachable from root 0.

Contract {1,2}. Entering via 0→1 replaces the chosen incoming arc 2→1,
so its reduced cost is 5−1=4. Entering via 0→2 instead costs 6−1=5.
The contracted problem chooses the original arc 0→1. Expansion removes
2→1 and keeps 1→2, giving total cost 5+1=6. The table and drawing use
actual phase records and the recovered original tree.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/chu_liu_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<dm::algorithms::WeightedEdge> edges{{0,1,5},{0,2,6},{1,2,1},{2,1,1}};
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::chu_liu_edmonds_trace(3,edges,0);
  if(!t.tree.result.exists || t.tree.result.total_weight!=6 || t.phases.size()!=2)return 1;
  std::print("| phase | current vertex | chosen original arc id | original endpoints | working cost |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t p=0;p<t.phases.size();++p)for(std::size_t v=0;v<t.phases[p].vertex_count;++v)if(v!=t.phases[p].root) {
    const auto id=t.phases[p].incoming_edges[v];const auto [u,w,cost]=edges[id];
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} -> {} | {} |\n",p,v,id,u,w,t.phases[p].incoming_weights[v]);
  }
  std::print("\nRecovered parents: {}. Original selected ids for vertices 1,2: {},{}.\n",t.tree.parent,t.tree.incoming_edges[1],t.tree.incoming_edges[2]);
  std::print("Reduced total {} = original selected cost {}.\n",t.reduced_total,t.tree.result.total_weight);
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(60,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;node.circle=true;node.width=1.1;node.height=1.1;node.font_size=22;
  const std::array<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint,3> positions{{{0,0},{4,2},{4,-2}}};
  for(std::size_t v=0;v<3;++v){node.fill=v?dm::graphics::RGB{254,240,138}:dm::graphics::RGB{220,252,231};diagram.node(std::format("first{}",v),positions[v],std::format("{}",v),node);}
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke potential;potential.color={148,163,184};potential.dashed=true;potential.width=1.5;
  diagram.edge("first0","first1",std::format("{}",std::get<2>(edges[0])),potential)
      .edge("first0","first2",std::format("{}",std::get<2>(edges[1])),potential);
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke chosen;chosen.color={234,88,12};chosen.width=3;chosen.arrow=true;
  diagram.path({{4.4,1.6},{5.5,0},{4.4,-1.6}},chosen).text({5.8,0},std::format("{}",std::get<2>(edges[t.phases[0].incoming_edges[2]])),20)
      .path({{3.6,-1.6},{2.5,0},{3.6,1.6}},chosen).text({2.1,0},std::format("{}",std::get<2>(edges[t.phases[0].incoming_edges[1]])),20);
  node.fill={220,252,231};diagram.node("root",{10,0},"0",node);node.fill={254,240,138};node.width=2;node.height=2;
  diagram.node("cycle",{16,0},"{1,2}",node);
  chosen.color={37,99,235};
  diagram.path({{10.5,0.4},{13,1.5},{15.05,0.4}},chosen).text({13,2},std::format("reduced {}",t.phases[1].edges[0].weight),20);
  potential.arrow=true;
  diagram.path({{10.5,-0.4},{13,-1.5},{15.05,-0.4}},potential).text({13,-2},std::format("reduced {}",t.phases[1].edges[1].weight),20);
  diagram.text({2,4.3},"Cheapest incoming arcs: a cycle",21)
      .text({13,4.3},std::format("Contract; baseline {}",t.phases[0].added_cost),21)
      .text({8,-4.5},"Expand the chosen entry: replace 2 -> 1 by 0 -> 1",20);
  node.width=1.1;node.height=1.1;
  for(std::size_t v=0;v<3;++v){node.fill=v?dm::graphics::RGB{219,234,254}:dm::graphics::RGB{220,252,231};diagram.node(std::format("tree{}",v),{7.0*v,-9},std::format("{}",v),node);}
  for(std::size_t v=1;v<3;++v)diagram.edge(std::format("tree{}",t.tree.parent[v]),std::format("tree{}",v),std::format("original cost {}",std::get<2>(edges[t.tree.incoming_edges[v]])));
  diagram.text({7,-6.7},std::format("Recovered original tree, cost {}",t.tree.result.total_weight),22).save_svg("build/chu_liu_method.svg");
