\caption(The exact known optimum and named 6k edge-visit count hold across the controlled family.)
\alttext(A blue line of actual combined incoming/reweight inspections coincides with orange 6k prediction points as cycle size grows.)

For P rounds, this implementation performs O(P(V+E)) work, with P≤V because
every nonfinal contraction reduces the current vertex count. The familiar
O(VE) bound applies when E is at least V−1, as it must be for a feasible
spanning graph; the V term still matters for sparse impossible inputs.
Compact expansion maps require O(E+PV) auxiliary storage even for the legacy
cost-returning call. Full tracing additionally retains arcs and partitions for
O(P(V+E)) storage. The old cost-only implementation did not recover edges;
this implementation's expansion history is part of its memory cost.
No observational dataset is needed for these controlled graph identities.

> Nonexistence is not a partial branching

An isolated vertex without an incoming arc fails immediately. A closed cycle
unreachable from the root can give every non-root vertex an initial incoming
choice, yet fails after contraction. A finite edge entering the root cannot
make that cycle reachable from the root. The returned legacy failure is
{total_weight=0, exists=false}; recovered parent/edge arrays are empty.
The trace still retains the actual failed round and any earlier reduced baseline.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const std::vector<std::vector<dm::algorithms::WeightedEdge>> graphs{
      {{0,1,1}},{{1,2,1},{2,1,1}},{{1,0,-9},{1,2,1},{2,1,1}}};
  const std::array<std::string,3> names{"initial missing vertex","closed unreachable cycle","cycle with arc into root"};
  std::print("| input | exists | rounds | final missing current vertices | reduced prefix | returned cost |\n| :--- | :--- | ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<graphs.size();++i) {
    const auto t=dm::algorithms::chu_liu_edmonds_trace(3,graphs[i],0);
    if(t.tree.result.exists || !t.tree.parent.empty() || t.phases.back().missing_vertices.empty())return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",names[i],t.tree.result.exists,t.work.phases,t.phases.back().missing_vertices,t.reduced_total,t.tree.result.total_weight);
  }
  const auto signed_tree=dm::algorithms::chu_liu_edmonds_tree(2,{{1,1,-100},{1,0,-100},{0,1,-3},{0,1,-3}},0);
  if(signed_tree.result.total_weight!=-3 || signed_tree.incoming_edges[1]!=2)return 1;
  std::print("\nNegative parallel control: cost {}, chosen original id {}; self loop and root-entering arc ignored after validation.\n",signed_tree.result.total_weight,signed_tree.incoming_edges[1]);
}
