\caption(Failed graphs retain no partial recovered tree; negative finite costs, ignored arcs and parallel tie identities have separate contracts.)

Every endpoint and weight validates before caps or algorithmic selection,
including arcs that will be ignored. NaN and infinities reject explicitly;
absence is represented by omitting an arc, not by an infinite weight. Equal
working costs prefer the first original input edge. Parallel input arcs remain
separate throughout contraction, selection and expansion. Root self-parenting
in the returned parent array is a storage convention, not a selected self loop.

> Work caps and finite-range arithmetic

Positive BranchingOptions caps bound actual rounds and the combined incoming
and reweight edge inspections across the whole call. Zero disables the
respective cap. The original example needs two rounds and twelve named visits:
eight for incoming choices and four for contraction. Validation is counted
separately. Recovery copies and parent walks are outside the edge-visit cap;
these controls are not a complete memory budget. Exhaustion throws
std::length_error and exposes no partial result.

A working reduced cost can exceed double range even when the recovered
original total fits. Costs and differences therefore use checked long double,
then the selected original edges are summed in original destination order and
checked before conversion to the unchanged double result field. The reduced
baseline total is retained separately; floating roundoff can make it differ
from the sum of the recovered original edges. This is numerical optimisation,
not an exact-real optimality certificate or arbitrary-precision arithmetic.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const std::vector<dm::algorithms::WeightedEdge> edges{{0,1,5},{0,2,6},{1,2,1},{2,1,1}};
  dm::algorithms::BranchingOptions exact;exact.max_phases=2;exact.max_edge_visits=12;
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::chu_liu_edmonds_trace(3,edges,0,exact);
  auto low=exact;low.max_phases=1;bool phase_cap=false;
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::chu_liu_edmonds_tree(3,edges,0,low);}catch(const std::length_error&){phase_cap=true;}
  low=exact;low.max_edge_visits=11;bool visit_cap=false;
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::chu_liu_edmonds_trace(3,edges,0,low);}catch(const std::length_error&){visit_cap=true;}
  bool invalid=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::chu_liu_edmonds_tree(2,{{0,1,1},{1,0,std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN()}},0,low);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){invalid=true;}
  if(t.tree.result.total_weight!=6 || !phase_cap || !visit_cap || !invalid)return 1;
  std::print("Exact caps return cost {}. One-below phase cap rejects: {}. One-below visit cap rejects: {}.\n",t.tree.result.total_weight,phase_cap,visit_cap);
  std::print("Ignored root-entering NaN rejects during full validation: {}.\n",invalid);
  const auto m=std::numeric_limits<double>::max();
  const auto wide=dm::algorithms::chu_liu_edmonds_trace(3,{{0,1,m},{0,2,m},{1,2,-m},{2,1,-m}},0);
  if(wide.tree.result.total_weight!=0 || wide.phases[1].edges[0].weight<=m)return 1;
  std::print("Wide reduced entry / DBL_MAX = {}; recovered original cost {}.\n",wide.phases[1].edges[0].weight/m,wide.tree.result.total_weight);
  bool overflow=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::chu_liu_edmonds(3,{{0,1,m},{0,2,m}},0);}catch(const std::overflow_error&){overflow=true;}
  if(!overflow)return 1;std::print("Unrepresentable final original total throws overflow_error: {}.\n",overflow);
  const auto one=dm::algorithms::chu_liu_edmonds_tree(1,{},0);
  std::print("Singleton root: parents {}, cost {}.\n",one.parent,one.result.total_weight);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Exact caps return cost 6. One-below phase cap rejects: true. One-below visit cap rejects: true.
Ignored root-entering NaN rejects during full validation: true.
